{% doc %}
  Judge.me mount points for the product page.

  Judge.me publishes each product's star badge and review list as metafields,
  which is the supported way to place them inside theme markup rather than
  wherever the app decides to inject them.

  The carousel and the all-reviews list are not here. Those are Judge.me app
  blocks, added in the theme editor, and a theme cannot render them by writing
  their markup by hand: an empty div with a jdgm class is not something their
  script fills in. sections/reviews-carousel.liquid and reviews-all.liquid
  hold the slot for those blocks instead.

  Nothing is output unless Judge.me is switched on in theme settings, so an
  uninstalled shop shows no empty boxes.

  @param {string} type - badge or widget
  @param {product} product

  @example
  {% render 'judgeme', type: 'badge', product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if settings.enable_judgeme -%}
  {%- case type -%}
    {%- when 'badge' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Star rating. Sits near the price and on product cards. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge" data-id="{{ product.id }}">
        {{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge }}
      </div>

    {%- when 'widget' -%}
      {%- comment -%} The full review list and the write-a-review form. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="jdgm-widget jdgm-review-widget" data-id="{{ product.id }}" data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}">
        {{ product.metafields.judgeme.widget }}
      </div>
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
